# Styling & the design canvas

Full write-up (read before building/adjusting screens): `.claude/skills/styling-design-canvas/SKILL.md`.

`View/Components/ClassicalTheme.axaml` defines every design token (`ColorBg`,
`ColorAccent`, `ColorScrim`, `Heading1`, `Kicker`, `Chip`, `TagSign`,
`ClassicInput`, the stroked 24×24 `Icon*` geometries…). **Bind to these — no raw
hex, font names or ad-hoc sizes in views.**

## The 720 canvas and its scale factors

- Layouts are authored against a **720**-wide canvas, nominally **720×1560**.
  Pixel values are the source design's px scaled by **~1.7476**. Follow that
  factor rather than eyeballing.
- **Type carries a further ×1.1 on top of that factor**, as do the controls
  sized around it (`VButton` heights, input `MinHeight`, the `FormInput` combo
  and date-picker heights). A new font size taken straight from the source
  design reads a step small — multiply it too. Geometry with no text (icons,
  dividers, avatar circles, the bottom bar's 100-unit row) is **unscaled** and
  stays on the plain factor.
- Scaling is by `Components/DesignCanvas.cs`, **not a `Viewbox`** (a Viewbox
  letterboxes non-720:1560 devices against `ShellView`'s black background).
  `DesignCanvas` scales by width (width is always exact; leftover height becomes
  extra canvas), falling back to centred height-capped scaling on wide displays.

## Rules for new screens

- **Never pin a root `Height`.** Set `Width="720"`, let height stretch, put
  content in a `ScrollViewer`. Only the three `NavigationController` screens
  (`LoginView`, `SignUpView`, `MainView`) carry a `DesignCanvas`; everything
  shown through `CurrentView` sits inside `MainView`'s and **must not add its own**.
- **Popup content is not scaled by the canvas** (`DesignCanvas` uses a
  `RenderTransform`, which doesn't affect layout; a popup lays out in its own
  visual root at scale 1). A drop-down is ~2.8× too wide at phone scale.
  - Dog/tutor pickers → **`inputs:VSearchableComboBox`** (lists matches inline in
    ordinary layout), styled `Classes="FormInput"`.
  - Stock `ComboBox`/`CalendarDatePicker` still open real popups — tolerable
    only because their content is short and theme-sized; **do not put a
    canvas-sized `FontSize` in their item templates.**
- Inputs/buttons come from AvaloniaFramework (`inputs:VTextBoxWithLabel`,
  `buttons:VButton`, `buttons:GroupButton`), themed via `V*` properties on a
  style class in `ClassicalTheme.axaml`, not inline.
- `App.axaml` must include `<framework:LayoutStyles />` or those controls render
  untemplated — check this first if a control looks unstyled.
- Compiled bindings are on: **every `.axaml` needs `x:DataType`.**
- Icons are stroked, never filled — one geometry serves muted and accent by
  following `Foreground`.

## ConfirmDialog

`View/Components/ConfirmDialog.axaml` is the app's modal (destructive confirms
and alerts): a scrim over the hosting screen, not a window (the app is
single-view on mobile). Add it as the **last child of a screen's root `Grid`**.
Confirm form `Sim`/`Não`; alert form `ShowCancel="False"` + `ConfirmText`. Its
internal bindings use `{Binding #Root.X}` — a plain `{Binding X}` would resolve
against the screen's view model (a `UserControl` inherits its parent's
`DataContext`).

Related: `avalonia-docs-connector` (verify Avalonia 12.1.1 XAML before editing)
and `navigation-presentation` (`CurrentView` vs the three canvas-bearing screens).
